  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Operate",
    "overview": "A compact native switchboard of projects and worktrees. Kossé is read briefly beside an editor or terminal: recognise a service, inspect its identity, open it or explicitly confirm a stop. Neutral surfaces keep process facts prominent; Québec-inspired blue identifies primary actions and selected form choices.\n\nThis records the owner-approved native replacement of the retired browser dashboard. It was a code-led operational port, without a seeded concept roll or an approved composition. There is no retrospective seed, quality score or claim of visual approval. The authority is `crates/app/src/native/view.rs`, `customize.rs`, `customize/form.rs` and `customize/fields.rs`, with Rune and rune-kit pinned to `b63efb3d`. Earlier review screenshots predate the final density and blue-control changes. The surface composition is recorded separately in [.impeccable/surfaces/native.md](.impeccable/surfaces/native.md).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact project groups with stable process identity.",
      "Neutral light and dark appearance with a single action accent.",
      "Explicit observation text and quiet, current metrics.",
      "Structured customization with visible inheritance and a fixed save footer."
